<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Doubravka of Bohemia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 977</span> · Also known as Dobrawa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Doubravka (d. 977) was a Bohemian princess, a daughter of Duke Boleslaus I, who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-i">Mieszko I of Poland</a> in 965. Her marriage was linked to Mieszko's baptism in 966, which brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Christendom</a>. She was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/doubravka-of-bohemia.jpg" alt="Doubravka of Bohemia" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Matejko · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dobrawa_(274945).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
